# 🗄️ AniList Automated Backup (`anilist-backup`)

![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)
![Built by AI](https://img.shields.io/badge/Built%20With-AI-blueviolet.svg)
![Sync Interval](https://img.shields.io/badge/Sync-Every%205%20Minutes-blue.svg)

An automated, self-updating, public JSON mirror of the **AniList Anime & Manga catalog**, powered by GitHub Actions.

Designed as a high-availability fallback dataset so developers, websites, Discord bots, and apps can continue reading Anime and Manga metadata even when the official AniList API (`graphql.anilist.co`) or Cloudflare is experiencing downtime.

> 🤖 **AI-Generated Project Notice:**  
> This repository—including its sharded architecture, GraphQL cursor/windowing sync script (`sync.py`), fault-tolerant GitHub Actions pipeline, and documentation—was **created by AI** in collaboration with [@thaware12](https://github.com/thaware12).

> 🔓 **100% Free & Open (MIT License):**  
> This repository and all backed-up metadata structure are **completely free to use for everyone** (personal, open-source, or commercial projects) under the **MIT License**.

---

## ✨ How It Works

1. **Phase 1 — Initial Full Catalog Seed:**
   - Queries AniList's GraphQL API in ID windows (`id_in`) of 500 IDs at a time (`MAX_REQUESTS_PER_RUN = 75`) to respect AniList's 30 req/min rate limit and bypass the 5,000-item pagination depth cap.
   - Commits progress after every run to `state.json` until the entire catalog is backed up.
2. **Phase 2 — 5-Minute Incremental Delta Sync:**
   - Once `"seed_complete": true` is reached in `state.json`, the GitHub Action runs on a `*/5 * * * *` cron schedule and queries `media(sort: UPDATED_AT_DESC)`.
   - It fetches **only newly added or recently modified entries** since the `last_updated_at` Unix timestamp watermark and overwrites **only those changed IDs** inside their respective shard files while keeping all existing data intact.
3. **Outage-Resilient Error Handling:**
   - If AniList is down or Cloudflare blocks requests (`HTTP 403`, `429`, `500`, `502`, `503`, `504`, `520–524`, or network timeout), the script safely saves any in-memory progress and exits with code `0` so the existing backup stays untouched and workflows do not spam failure emails.
   - Real code or GraphQL schema bugs exit with code `1` to alert the maintainer.

---

## 📂 Repository & Sharding Structure

To stay well below GitHub's 100 MB file size limit and keep file lookups fast, media entries are grouped into **shards of 1,000 IDs** using integer division (`Math.floor(id / 1000)` padded to 4 digits):

```text
anilist-backup/
├── .github/workflows/
│   └── sync.yml                  # Runs every 5 minutes via GitHub Actions
├── data/
│   ├── anime/
│   │   ├── shard_0000.json       # Anime IDs 1 to 999
│   │   ├── shard_0001.json       # Anime IDs 1000 to 1999
│   │   └── ...
│   └── manga/
│       ├── shard_0030.json       # Manga IDs 30000 to 30999
│       └── ...
├── state.json                    # Sync watermark and progress tracker
├── sync.py                       # Main Python GraphQL sync engine
└── README.md
```

### How to Find Which File Holds an ID
$$\text{shard\_number} = \lfloor \text{id} \div 1000 \rfloor$$

- **Anime ID `1`** (*Cowboy Bebop*) $\rightarrow$ `0000` $\rightarrow$ `data/anime/shard_0000.json` (key `"1"`)
- **Anime ID `1535`** (*Death Note*) $\rightarrow$ `0001` $\rightarrow$ `data/anime/shard_0001.json` (key `"1535"`)
- **Anime ID `21459`** (*My Hero Academia*) $\rightarrow$ `0021` $\rightarrow$ `data/anime/shard_0021.json` (key `"21459"`)
- **Manga ID `30002`** (*Berserk*) $\rightarrow$ `0030` $\rightarrow$ `data/manga/shard_0030.json` (key `"30002"`)

---

## 📊 What Data Is Backed Up?

Each entry is keyed by its stringified AniList `id` inside its shard file and contains the following fields:

| Field | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | `Int` | AniList Media ID |
| `idMal` | `Int \| null` | MyAnimeList (MAL) ID |
| `type` | `String` | `"ANIME"` or `"MANGA"` |
| `format` | `String` | `"TV"`, `"TV_SHORT"`, `"MOVIE"`, `"SPECIAL"`, `"OVA"`, `"ONA"`, `"MUSIC"`, `"MANGA"`, `"NOVEL"`, `"ONE_SHOT"` |
| `status` | `String` | `"FINISHED"`, `"RELEASING"`, `"NOT_YET_RELEASED"`, `"CANCELLED"`, `"HIATUS"` |
| `updatedAt` | `Int` | Unix timestamp of the last update on AniList |
| `title` | `Object` | `{ "romaji": String, "english": String \| null, "native": String \| null }` |
| `episodes` | `Int \| null` | Total episodes (Anime) |
| `chapters` | `Int \| null` | Total chapters (Manga) |
| `volumes` | `Int \| null` | Total volumes (Manga) |
| `averageScore` | `Int \| null` | Average score out of 100 |
| `popularity` | `Int` | Number of users with this media on their list |
| `genres` | `String[]` | Array of genre names |

### Sample Entry (`data/anime/shard_0000.json` $\rightarrow$ `"1"`)
```json
{
  "1": {
    "averageScore": 86,
    "chapters": null,
    "episodes": 26,
    "format": "TV",
    "genres": [
      "Action",
      "Adventure",
      "Drama",
      "Sci-Fi"
    ],
    "id": 1,
    "idMal": 1,
    "popularity": 350000,
    "status": "FINISHED",
    "title": {
      "english": "Cowboy Bebop",
      "native": "カウボーイビバップ",
      "romaji": "Cowboy Bebop"
    },
    "type": "ANIME",
    "updatedAt": 1729670000,
    "volumes": null
  }
}
```

