## 🚀 How to Use This Backup in Your Projects

For production apps, use the free **jsDelivr CDN** (`cdn.jsdelivr.net`) so you never hit GitHub raw rate limits. For instant uncached reads, use `raw.githubusercontent.com`.

### 1. JavaScript / TypeScript (Automatic Fallback When AniList Is Down)

```javascript
async function getMediaWithFallback(id, mediaType = "anime") {
  const shardId = String(Math.floor(id / 1000)).padStart(4, "0");
  const backupUrl = `[https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/thaware12/anilist-backup@main/data/$](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/thaware12/anilist-backup@main/data/$){mediaType.toLowerCase()}/shard_${shardId}.json`;

  try {
    // 1. Try Official AniList GraphQL API first
    const response = await fetch("[https://graphql.anilist.co](https://graphql.anilist.co)", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Accept: "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        query: `query ($id: Int) {
          Media(id: $id) {
            id idMal type format status updatedAt
            title { romaji english native }
            episodes chapters volumes averageScore popularity genres
          }
        }`,
        variables: { id: Number(id) },
      }),
      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000),
    });

    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`AniList HTTP ${response.status}`);
    const payload = await response.json();
    if (payload.errors) throw new Error("AniList GraphQL Error");

    return { source: "anilist-live", data: payload.data.Media };
  } catch (error) {
    // 2. Fallback to GitHub Backup if AniList or Cloudflare is down
    console.warn(`AniList unavailable (${error.message}). Falling back to anilist-backup...`);
    const backupRes = await fetch(backupUrl);
    if (!backupRes.ok) throw new Error(`Shard ${shardId} not found in backup`);
    const shard = await backupRes.json();
    return { source: "github-backup", data: shard[String(id)] || null };
  }
}

// Example: Fetch Cowboy Bebop (ID: 1)
getMediaWithFallback(1, "anime").then(console.log);
```

### 2. Python

```python
import requests

def get_from_backup(media_id: int, media_type: str = "anime") -> dict | None:
    shard_id = f"{media_id // 1000:04d}"
    url = (
        f"[https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/thaware12/anilist-backup@main/](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/thaware12/anilist-backup@main/)"
        f"data/{media_type.lower()}/shard_{shard_id}.json"
    )
    response = requests.get(url, timeout=15)
    response.raise_for_status()
    shard_data = response.json()
    return shard_data.get(str(media_id))

# Example: Fetch Cowboy Bebop (ID: 1)
print(get_from_backup(1, "anime"))
```

